UID:0444d97093c6bba0@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART:20260910T220000Z
DTEND:20260910T233000Z
SUMMARY:So you want to start a family?  What to know about family law bef
 ore getting married or having children.
LOCATION:Masiello Classroom
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17185766
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Raising your children is a constitutional right.  Marriage is 
 a contract.  Come find out the terms before you sign\, with Keene Family L
 aw attorneys  Sofia Cunha-Vasconcelos and Lindsey Bramble. The program wil
 l address key points regarding marriage and having children in New Hampshi
 re for a majority of relationships\, recognizing that there are many diffe
 rent kinds of relationships and the laws in other states may differ.\n\nIn
 formation in this seminar is legal education\, not legal advice.  Attendan
 ce does not constitute the creation of an attorney client relationship.”
 \nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d1f504b7c5e8e673@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART:20260911T180000Z
DTEND:20260911T200000Z
SUMMARY:Create your own Rubber Stamp
LOCATION:Kingsbury Makerspace
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17237115
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will introduce you to materials and processes ne
 eded to create your own Ex Libris bookplate rubber stamp using the laser e
 ngraver and the 3d printer. \n\nTo participate in this workshop you must c
 omplete the online tutorial: Introduction to the Makerspace and the Epilog
  Laser Engraver Certification Tutorial.  Both tutorials can be found here:
  https://my.nicheacademy.com/makerspacetutorials\n\nPlease complete both o
 f these tutorials by Tuesday September 1st. If you have trouble accessing 
 the tutorials or have questions please call the makerspace directly (603 7
 57-0621) and leave a message. We will respond within 48 hours. If you do n
 ot complete the tutorials by this date your reservation will be cancelled 
 and opened to a person on the wait-list.\n\nFor more information contact A
 my Kraemer akraemer@keenenh.gov\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
