UID:6666fb94464e16c4@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART:20260923T213000Z
DTEND:20260923T233000Z
SUMMARY:Learn to 3D Print at the Kingsbury Makerspace - Workshop
LOCATION:Kingsbury Makerspace
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17180252
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Learn what you can make with our 3D Printers! This workshop wi
 ll provide you with all the information you need to start 3D Printing\, an
 d walk you through a hands-on activity to 3D Print your own bookmark. All 
 materials are provided. \n\nTo participate in this workshop you must compl
 ete the online tutorial: Introduction to the Makerspace and the 3D Printer
  Certification Tutorial.  Both tutorials can be found here: https://my.nic
 heacademy.com/makerspacetutorials\n\nPlease complete both of these tutoria
 ls by Tuesday Sept. 15. If you do not complete the tutorials by this date 
 your reservation will be cancelled and opened to a person on the wait list
 .\n\nThis workshop is intended to introduce our 3D Printers to new users. 
 If you have questions please contact A Welby at awelby@keenenh.gov or Amy 
 Kraemer at akraemer@keenenh.gov\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5f8de4eef51f5300@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART:20260924T220000Z
DTEND:20260924T230000Z
SUMMARY:Walking the White Blazes: Exploring the Appalachian Trail
LOCATION:Ruth Huntress Auditorium
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17178782
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Stretching over 2\,190 miles from Georgia to Maine\, the Appal
 achian Trail is one of the world's most famous footpath journeys. Join us 
 for an engaging presentation that traces the history\, landscapes\, and cu
 lture of "the A.T."\n\nWe’ll explore the rich origins of the trail\, jou
 rney through the 14 states it traverses\, and highlight the diverse flora 
 and fauna—from mountain laurels to black bears—that hikers encounter a
 long the way. You’ll also learn unique trail lingo like thru-hiking\, tr
 ail magic\, and zero days. Whether you're an experienced backpacker\, a ca
 sual day-hiker\, or an armchair traveler\, you'll leave with a deeper appr
 eciation for this iconic American treasure.\n\nPresented by Jay Fee\, who 
 hiked the Appalachian Trail in 2000\, and is now Library Systems Administr
 ator for the Keene Public Library.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a52d984069a27ba4@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART:20260926T140000Z
DTEND:20260926T160000Z
SUMMARY:Courageous Conversation Workshop
LOCATION:Heberton Hall
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17509086
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:The Courageous Conversation Workshop is a hands-on workshop wh
 ere you will practice the skills that make difficult conversations more pr
 oductive\, more respectful and more human. Through guided activities\, rol
 e-playing and real life scenarios\, you will build confidence to navigate 
 disagreement with curiosity instead of conflict. Presented by the Monadnoc
 k Diversity\, Equity\, Inclusion and Belonging Coalition. \n\nRegistration
  is appreciated.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
