BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3c5b8613a0d5672f@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART:20261009T203000Z
DTEND:20261009T213000Z
SUMMARY:Kids Comic Club
LOCATION:Kay Fox Room
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17442891
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:For comic fans ages 8-12! We'll meet once a month to create to
 gether\, discuss great graphic novels\, and watch interviews and tutorials
  from our favorite artists. All skill levels are welcome\, and materials w
 ill be provided! Meetings will be held on the second Friday of each month.
 \n\nRegistration is appreciated. Questions or Concerns call the library 60
 3.352.0157.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f7314da25e20b92a@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART:20261010T150000Z
DTEND:20261010T163000Z
SUMMARY:Mel Allen Author talk Listening to New England
LOCATION:Heberton Hall
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/16326529
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:We are very happy to host long-time writer and editor of Yanke
 e magazine\, Mel Allen. "Listening to New England" is a 45-minute talk wit
 h images from Mel's nearly half-centrury of reporting and writing about th
 e unique people and places of New England for Yankee Magazine. This emotiv
 e presentation will let you see and feel the region in a unique way.  He w
 ill talk about Yankee's past and how it has survived for 90 years since it
 s founding in 1935. There will be time for questions and answers after his
  presentation.\n\nToadstool Bookshop will be on hand selling Mel's newest 
 book Here in New England: Unforgettable people\, places and memories that 
 connect us all. Mel will be happy to sign your copy. \n\nYou can listen to
  NPR's "Here and Now" interview with Mel about Here in New England.\n\nThe
  Keene Public Library has a nearly complete archive of Yankee Magazine for
  people to look through.  Just ask at the reference desk.\n\nFor more info
 rmation\, please contact Amy Kraemer: akraemer@keenenh.gov\nSource: Keene 
 Public Library
END:VEVENT
