BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2ffee80f4c14d708@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T200000
SUMMARY:Joyriding: Sex\, Drugs and Adventure on the 1970s Gringo Trail - B
 ook Launch with Joyce Marcel
LOCATION:Main Reading Room
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/joyriding-sex-drugs-and-adventure-on
 -the-1970s-gringo-trail-book-launch-with-joyce-marcel/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:All are welcome to the formal roll-out of Joyce Marcel’s new
  book\, Joyriding: Sex\, Drugs and Adventure on the 1970s Gringo Trail\, b
 eing held in the Main Reading Room at 6:30 p.m. on Wednesday\, September 9
 th. \nMarcel\, one of Vermont’s best-known journalists\, will be intervi
 ewed by someone who knows her well\, her husband\, The Commons news editor
  Randy Holhut. They will talk about the adventures she describes in her bo
 ok — which include galloping a race horse up a snow-capped volcano\, bei
 ng cured of hepatitis by a witch doctor\, and\, improbably\, becoming ship
 wrecked in the Amazon — as well as her creative process. \nThe talk will
  be recorded by BCTV and later broadcast on its Community Channel 1078 and
  website brattleboro.tv\, as well as on its YouTube page. \nWe hope you ca
 n join us for the stories and laughter in what promises to be an engaging 
 conversation and delightful event. \nSigned copies will be available for s
 ale. More about the book can be found on Joyce’s website: https://new.jo
 ycemarcel.com/\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c78fa1abbc58cc58@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260903T145711Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T190000
SUMMARY:Sci-Fi Film Series: EX MACHINA
LOCATION:The Latchis Theatre\, 50 Main Street\, Brattleboro\, Vermont\, 05
 301\, United States
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/sci-fi-film-series-ex-machina/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:The Sci-Fi Film Series is your chance to see great and classic
  Sci-Fi films on the big screen! Join us at the Latchis Theater to watch t
 his month’s film\, Ex Machina! \nCaleb Smith (Domhnall Gleeson)\, a prog
 rammer at an internet-search giant\, wins a competition to spend a week at
  the private mountain estate of the company’s brilliant and reclusive CE
 O\, Nathan Bateman (Oscar Isaac). Upon his arrival\, Caleb learns that Nat
 han has chosen him to be the human component in a Turing Test—charging h
 im with evaluating the capabilities\, and ultimately the consciousness\, o
 f Nathan’s latest experiment in artificial intelligence. That experiment
  is Ava (Alicia Vikander)\, a breathtaking A.I. whose emotional intelligen
 ce proves more sophisticated––and more deceptive––than the two men
  could have imagined. \nAttendees are invited to stay afterward for a disc
 ussion about the film. Admission by donation. \nPresented by Brooks Memori
 al Library and the Latchis Theater. Sponsored by the Friends of Brooks Mem
 orial Library.\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
